    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Distinguish static vs. dynamic: Weathering is purely an in-situ process, whereas erosion requires movement and transport.",
        "Contrast river vs. glacial valleys: River erosion produces V-shaped valleys, whereas glacial erosion forms U-shaped valleys.",
        "Arid landforms: Mushroom rocks and Yardangs are erosional wind features, while Sand dunes and Loess are depositional wind features.",
        "Marine landforms: Sea arches and Stacks are erosional marine landforms, while Beaches and Bars are depositional marine features."
      ],
      "id": "cpyr9wu"
